n start using `chakin` by following these steps:\\n\\n1. **Import the Library**:  \\n   In your Python script, import `chakin` using:\\n   ```python\\n   import chakin\\n   ```\\n\\n2. **Download Word Vectors**:  \\n   Use the appropriate function to download the desired word vectors. For example:\\n   ```python\\n   chakin.download(\'word_vector_name\')\\n   ```\\n\\n3. **Load Word Vectors**:  \\n   Load the downloaded vectors into your application:\\n   ```python\\n   vectors = chakin.load(\'path_to_vectors\')\\n   ```\\n\\n4. **Utilize Word Vectors**:  \\n   Now you can use the loaded word vectors for your NLP tasks.\\n\\n## Conclusion\\nBy following this manual, you should be able to efficiently set up and utilize `chakin` for your NLP applications. For further assistance, please refer to the official documentation or contact the support team.\\n","encoding":"utf-8","mode":"overwrite"}', call_id='call_kdk3UcnFW74KRNQO9lJNuG5q', name='save_file', type='function_call', id='fc_tmp_ezk88jijllr', namespace=None, status='completed')], parallel_tool_calls=True, temperature=0.7, tool_choice='auto', tools=[FunctionTool(name='init_python_env', parameters={'type': 'object', 'properties': {'python_version': {'type': 'string', 'default': None}}}, strict=None, type='function', defer_loading=None, description='Run uv lock and uv venv inside the workspace.'), FunctionTool(name='install_python_packages', parameters={'type': 'object', 'properties': {'packages': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}}, 'upgrade': {'type': 'boolean', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['packages']}, strict=None, type='function', defer_loading=None, description='Install Python packages inside the workspace using uv add.'), FunctionTool(name='uv_run', parameters={'type': 'object', 'properties': {'module': {'type': 'string', 'default': None}, 'script': {'type': 'string', 'default': None}, 'args': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'default': None}, 'env': {'type': 'object', 'default': 